WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.200
Gate one is Azure Service Health.

2
00:00:02.200 --> 00:00:06.299
Resource Graph answers the same
questions for every subscription

3
00:00:06.299 --> 00:00:10.325
in scope with one query, and
Microsoft Learn publishes the queries.

4
00:00:10.325 --> 00:00:11.337
Four steps.

5
00:00:11.337 --> 00:00:14.293
A subscription owner grants
the reader two roles:

6
00:00:14.293 --> 00:00:16.888
Reader, and Service
Health Security Reader.

7
00:00:16.888 --> 00:00:21.055
Learn explains why the second one
matters: with Reader alone you see a

8
00:00:21.055 --> 00:00:25.662
security advisory, but not its sensitive
fields or the resources it affects.

9
00:00:25.662 --> 00:00:29.788
Then sign in to the right cloud,
with the Resource Graph extension.

10
00:00:29.788 --> 00:00:34.688
The workbook's estate is GCC with
commercial Azure, so that's Azure Cloud.

11
00:00:34.688 --> 00:00:36.000
Third, collect.

12
00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.688
The kit's query starts from Learn's
sample for all active events.

13
00:00:39.688 --> 00:00:43.386
Fourth, alert between collections
with Learn's built-in policy,

14
00:00:43.386 --> 00:00:46.800
assigned at the management
group with a remediation task.

15
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.301
The kit writes it as a plan,

16
00:00:48.301 --> 00:00:51.940
and applies it only with the
hash the change record approved.
